: true` in `mcp_config.json`. When the user reported the popup still appeared on restart, completely deleted the `nexlev` block from the IDE's `mcp_config.json`.\n\n# 4. Model Knowledge\n### NexLev Startup Popup Issue\n- **The Problem:** The IDE auto-initializes all servers in `mcp_config.json` on startup. Because `mcp-remote` requires an OAuth browser flow, this was forcing an auth window open every single time the IDE launched. \n- **The Solution:** The `\"nexlev\"` block must be *completely removed* from `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\mcp_config.json`. The `\"disabled\": true` flag did not work.\n- **Why it still works:** Our `nexlev-mcp-caller` skill scripts do not rely on the IDE's MCP manager. They hardcode the server URL (`https://prod.dashboard.nexlev.io/api/claude-mcp`) and spawn their own connection, so removing it from the IDE config breaks nothing for us.\n\n### NexLev Python Caller Mechanics\n- Scripts are located at `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\scripts\\`.\n- Always write arguments to a temporary file (e.g., `$env:TEMP\\nexlev_args.json`) and pass the file path to the python script to avoid PowerShell mangling JSON quotes.\n- Once authenticated, tokens are cached globally by the npm package.\n\n# 5. Files and Code\n\n**Edited Files:**\n- `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\mcp_config.json`\n  - *What:* Completely deleted the `\"nexlev\"` configuration block.\n  - *Why:* To stop the IDE from auto-launching `mcp-remote` on startup and triggering annoying OAuth browser popups.\n- `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\SKILL.md`\n  - *What:* Created instructions for the agent on how to use the custom NexLev scripts, plus rate limit tables.\n- `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-caller\\scripts\\nexlev_call.py`\n  - *What:* Created single-tool caller script. Added UTF-8 stdout wrapper and `utf-8-sig` file reading.\n- `C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\config\\skills\\nexlev-mcp-calle